# No files in Documents

Adam’s `~/Documents` and `~/Desktop` are iCloud Drive. Git objects there go dataless and hang. **Do not create, clone, write, or worktree anything under those folders.** Codex/Claude default output paths under Documents are forbidden.

## Put code here

| Thing | Path |
|-------|------|
| Design kit | `/Users/adamrussell/Projects/hub-design-kit` |
| Teaching Hub | `/Users/adamrussell/Teaching Hub` |
| Knowledge Hub | `/Users/adamrussell/Projects/knowledge-hub` |
| Life Hub | `/Users/adamrussell/Projects/life-hub` |
| Tasks Hub | `/Users/adamrussell/Projects/tasks-hub` |
| New git repos | `/Users/adamrussell/Projects/<name>` |

If the workspace path contains `/Documents/` or `/Desktop/`: stop. Tell Adam. Relocate to `~/Projects/<name>` (or Teaching Hub), then `move_agent_to_root`. Do not keep editing in place except to finish a move.

## Put data here

- Source: git remotes (GitHub).
- Media, archives, exports, dumps, large binaries: **Cloudflare R2** (hub Workers/bindings). Not `~/Documents`, not repo `data/` dumps that belong in R2.

## Sites never depend on this Mac

Teaching, Knowledge, Life, Tasks, and future hubs must **never** need iCloud or any local file to work. Runtime data is git remotes + Cloudflare (Workers, R2, KV, D1). Do not add features that read `~/Documents`, `~/Desktop`, or other machine-local paths in production or as a required fallback.

